- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged unused dependencies but not the workspace = true pattern.
    Dev added chrono and uuid inline in Cargo.toml. No phase caught the version drift
    risk from inline dependency versions.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase mentioned FieldErrorCode or #[non_exhaustive] on any enum in
    the new code.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer LOW finding: 'Meta::new() generates trace_id as random UUID\
    \ \u2014 not propagated from request' and 'X-Request-Id header sent by clients\
    \ is ignored... trace correlation across services is impossible.'"
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer MEDIUM finding: 'No structured logging / tracing anywhere \u2014\
    \ zero observability. Not a single tracing::info!, tracing::debug!, or structured\
    \ span in the entire crate.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged misleading SECURITY comments claiming logging that doesn't
    exist.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote auth middleware tests for malformed headers but none specifically
    testing non-ASCII characters in X-Tenant-ID header.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-209 tests but the security tests only check status codes
    and generic messages, not response body content assertions for sensitive data
    leakage.
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer LOW finding: 'CORS is not implemented \u2014 OPTIONS returns\
    \ 404 via fallback. The test options_request_returns_cors_headers passes because\
    \ it accepts 404 as valid.'"
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged zero logging (I4) but since no logging was added, the
    wrong-log-level issue never materialized to be caught.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer LOW finding: 'CORS is not implemented \u2014 OPTIONS returns\
    \ 404 via fallback.' However, the reviewer noted the absence of CORS middleware\
